// Imports are FILE-scoped (SPEC §"Modules"), and UFCS follows them: a modifier
// list's exclusion binds the file that wrote it, and only that file.
//
// This file wildcard-imports `snippet/provider` with no modifiers, so `bump` is
// in scope here. Its sibling `other.vader` drops `bump` from its own wildcard,
// and the T3009 in the snapshot is that sibling's `c.bump()` — not this file's,
// which resolves. Before per-file overload tables the sibling's call resolved
// too (one table for the whole module), which is the divergence SPEC §UFCS
// rules out.
//
// The snapshot's second entry — R2006 on `bump(c)` BELOW, in a file that
// imports the name — is a KNOWN REMAINING BUG, kept visible on purpose. The
// resolver still seeds unqualified names per MODULE, unioning every file's
// exclusions, so the bare form is refused here while the UFCS form on the line
// above resolves: the same bare-vs-UFCS divergence, now surviving only on the
// resolver side. Closing it is the `files[0]`-only / per-file-seed work
// (TODO §1.13d); when that lands, this R2006 disappears and the snapshot moves.

module "snippet"

import "snippet/provider"

main :: fn() -> i32 {
    c :: Counter { .n = 0 }
    _ :: c.bump()
    _ :: bump(c)
    return from_sibling()
}
